; Litmus tests for the five atomic primitives, run on two threads, three
; for wrc, isa2 and 3.sb, or four for iriw.
;
; `scripts/check-atomics.sh` builds this with `--threads` and runs it
; once per row below; each run prints one line, `<forbidden>
; <witnessed>`, and the gate decides. Fifteen families, each with the
; outcome sequential consistency FORBIDS:
;
;   sb   store buffering. T0 stores x then loads y, T1 stores y then
;        loads x; forbidden is both loads answering 0. `sc` uses
;        `__atomic_store`/`__atomic_load`, `fence` plain accesses with
;        `__fence` between, `plain` plain accesses alone - the CONTROL,
;        which must show the forbidden outcome, or the zeros above it
;        mean only that this harness cannot see a reordering at all.
;   mp   message passing. T0 stores data (plain) then flag, T1 loads
;        flag and, if it is set, data (plain); forbidden is flag 1 with
;        data 0. `sc`
;        publishes through the atomic flag - the pattern a program
;        would actually use - `plain` makes the flag plain too, and
;        `fence` keeps it plain with `__fence` between each side's two
;        accesses. `reorder` is the control: with the atomics, T1 loads
;        data first, then the flag once it is stored.
;        The witness is how many rounds saw the flag at all: a run in
;        which T1 always read the flag first is not a test.
;   add  two threads each add 1 to one word `n` times; forbidden is
;        any lost update. `sc` is `__atomic_add`, `cas` a
;        compare-and-swap loop (witness: failed swaps, so contention
;        is shown rather than assumed), and `split` an atomic load
;        followed by an atomic store - atomic accesses, non-atomic
;        increment - the control that shows the threads overlap.
;   lb   load buffering. T0 loads x then stores y, T1 loads y then
;        stores x; forbidden is both loads answering 1. The witness is
;        the rounds in which both answered 0: both loads ran before
;        either store, so the threads overlapped.
;   2+2w two writes each. T0 stores x 1 then y 2, T1 stores y 1 then
;        x 2; forbidden is x 1 and y 1 after the join. The witness is
;        the rounds that ended x 2 and y 2, whose stores interleaved.
;   iriw independent reads of independent writes, on four bindings. W0
;        stores x, W1 stores y, R2 loads x then y, R3 loads y then x;
;        forbidden is R2 seeing x without y while R3 sees y without x,
;        the readers disagreeing on which write came first. The witness
;        is the rarer half of that, so both orders are seen, if never
;        in the same round. 200,000 rounds a run rather than 500,000,
;        because four threads cost more per round, and much more on a
;        host with fewer than four cores.
;   wrc  write-to-read causality, on three bindings. W stores x; R1
;        loads x, then stores y; R2 loads y, then x. Forbidden is R1
;        seeing x and R2 seeing y without x: R1's store, made after it
;        saw x, is visible while x is not. The witness is the rounds in
;        which R1 saw x and R2 saw y, the chain the outcome needs.
;   isa2 the same chain through three words. W stores x, then y; R1
;        loads y, then stores z; R2 loads z, then x. Forbidden is R1
;        seeing y and R2 seeing z without x; the witness is the rounds
;        in which R1 saw y and R2 saw z. Both run 200,000 rounds.
;
; In these five, `sc` uses the atomics, and `plain` the same accesses
; with `__load64`/`__store64` - the control, whose outcome the hardware
; may or may not show. `reorder` writes the reordering each family looks
; for into the program, with the atomics, so the forbidden outcome
; becomes one sequential consistency allows: lb stores before it loads,
; 2+2w swaps each thread's two stores, and iriw gives each reader its
; own copy of the other writer's word, stored after a pause, so W0
; reaches R2 first and W1 reaches R3 first. wrc's R2 loads x first and
; y once R1 has stored it. isa2's W stores y first and x after a pause,
; and its R2 loads x first and z once R1 has stored it. A
; `reorder` run that never shows the outcome means this harness could
; not see it happen.
;
; Three more families, r and s taking all four modes, `fence` among
; them, and 3.sb all but `fence`:
;   r    T0 stores x then y, T1 stores 2 to y then loads x; forbidden is
;        y ending 2 with T1's load answering 0. The witness is y ending
;        1 with the load answering 1, which only interleaved accesses
;        give.
;   s    T0 stores 2 to x then 1 to y, T1 loads y then stores 1 to x;
;        forbidden is x ending 2 with T1's load answering 1. The witness
;        is x ending 1 with the load answering 0, likewise.
;   3.sb store buffering around three bindings: each stores its own
;        word, then loads the next binding's. Forbidden is all three
;        loads answering 0. The witness is all three answering 1, the
;        one outcome no order of whole bindings gives. 200,000 rounds a
;        run.
; `fence` puts `__fence` between each binding's two plain accesses.
; `reorder` swaps T1's two accesses in r and s, with the atomics, and
; makes the second wait for T0's store to y; in 3.sb each binding loads,
; waits until all three have, then stores.
; The `plain` and `fence` rows' accesses race, which MM-PAR-9 leaves
; undefined, so they measure this compiler and this hardware.
;
; Four COHERENCE families, on one word x and two bindings. Coherence is
; the one ordering x86-64 and AArch64 give every aligned access, plain
; or atomic, so a `plain` run is expected to show nothing, and says
; nothing about the harness. Their `reorder` programs are the controls:
; each writes the violation into the program with the atomics.
;   corr two reads of one word may not go backwards. W stores 1; R loads
;        x twice. Forbidden is 1 then 0; the witness is 0 then 1, the
;        rounds whose reads straddled the store. `reorder` reports the
;        later load as the first.
;   coww two writes by one binding are seen in their order. W stores 1
;        then 2; R loads x twice. Forbidden is R seeing 2 then 1, or x
;        not ending with W's last store; the witness is the rounds in
;        which R saw x change. `reorder` stores 2, then 1.
;   cowr a binding reads its own write or a later one. W stores 1 then
;        loads x; O stores 2. Forbidden is W's load answering 0, or 2
;        while x ends 1 (O's store both after and before W's). The
;        witness is the rounds in which W read O's 2. `reorder` loads
;        before it stores, and only the second half is counted: a load
;        before any store may rightly answer 0.
;   corw a binding cannot read its own later write. W loads x then
;        stores 1; O stores 2. Forbidden is W's load answering 1, or 2
;        while x ends 2; the witness is the rounds in which W read O's 2.
;        `reorder` stores, then loads, and only the second half is
;        counted.
; A binding's two accesses to x are a pause apart in every mode, so the
; other binding's access lands between them often enough to count.
;
; Every round of every family but add uses FRESH zeroed words
; (MM-ALLOC-6), so no location is ever reset while another thread may
; still read it, and the threads meet at a spin barrier before each
; round so they start it together. What a zero here says is limited to
; the rounds run, on this host, at this `--opt`: the absence of an
; outcome is not a proof that it cannot happen.
(import Fmt)
(import IO)
(import Str)
(import Sys)

; Arrive at round `round`'s barrier and spin until both threads have.
; Answers the spin count, which nothing reads.
(:: arrive (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (arrive ctr round)
  (let (
    (mut spins 0)
    (want (* 2 (+ round 1)))
  )
    {
      (__atomic_add ctr 1)
      (while (< (__atomic_load ctr) want)
        (set spins (+ spins 1)))
      spins
    }))

; ---- sb ------------------------------------------------------------
; mode 0 sc, 1 plain, 2 fence. Writes round i's load into res[i].
(:: sbThread (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (sbThread mine other res ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 0)
            {
              (__atomic_store (+ mine (* 8 i)) 1)
              (__store64 res i (__atomic_load (+ other (* 8 i))))
            }
            (if (== mode 1)
              {
                (__store64 mine i 1)
                (__store64 res i (__load64 other i))
              }
              {
                (__store64 mine i 1)
                __fence
                (__store64 res i (__load64 other i))
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

(:: runSb (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runSb mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r0 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (sbThread
          xs
          ys
          r0
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (sbThread
          ys
          xs
          r1
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (if (== (+ (__load64 r0 i) (__load64 r1 i)) 0)
            (set weak (+ weak 1))
            0)
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (println (strConcat (fmtInt weak) (strConcat " " (fmtInt n))))
      0
    }))

; ---- mp ------------------------------------------------------------
; mode 0 sc (plain data, atomic flag), 1 plain, 2 fence (plain, with
; `__fence` between), 3 reorder (both stores atomic).
(:: mpWriter (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (mpWriter data flag ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 3)
            {
              (__atomic_store (+ data (* 8 i)) 1)
              (__atomic_store (+ flag (* 8 i)) 1)
            }
            {
              (__store64 data i 1)
              (if (== mode 0)
                (__atomic_store (+ flag (* 8 i)) 1)
                (if (== mode 2)
                  {
                    __fence
                    (__store64 flag i 1)
                  }
                  (__store64 flag i 1)))
            })
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; Round i's flag, through the atomic load (mode 0) or a plain one.
(:: loadFlag (-> Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (loadFlag flag i mode)
  (if (== mode 0)
    (__atomic_load (+ flag (* 8 i)))
    (__load64 flag i)))

; Writes the forbidden count to out[0] and the rounds that saw the
; flag to out[1]. `reorder` loads data first, with the atomics, then
; waits for the flag to be stored, for at most `waitSpins` loads, and
; loads it.
(:: mpReader (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (mpReader data flag ctr n mode out)
  (let (
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut seen 0)
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 3)
            (let ((d (__atomic_load (+ data (* 8 i)))))
              {
                (waitStored (+ flag (* 8 i)) waitSpins)
                (if (== (__atomic_load (+ flag (* 8 i))) 1)
                  {
                    (set seen (+ seen 1))
                    (if (== d 0)
                      (set weak (+ weak 1))
                      0)
                  }
                  0)
              })
            ; The data word is read only once the flag says it was
            ; published. Read before the test, it raced the writer's
            ; plain store whenever the flag was still 0 (MM-PAR-9), and
            ; ThreadSanitizer said so.
            (if (== (loadFlag flag i mode) 1)
              {
                (set seen (+ seen 1))
                (if (== mode 2)
                  __fence
                  0)
                (if (== (__load64 data i) 0)
                  (set weak (+ weak 1))
                  0)
              }
              0))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (__store64 out 0 weak)
      (__store64 out 1 seen)
      0
    }))

(:: runMp (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runMp mode n)
  (let (
    (data (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (flag (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (out (__alloc 16))
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (mpWriter
          data
          flag
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (mpReader
          data
          flag
          ctr
          n
          mode
          out))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (println (strConcat (fmtInt (__load64 out 0)) (strConcat " " (fmtInt (__load64 out 1)))))
      0
    }))

; ---- add -----------------------------------------------------------
; mode 0 sc, 1 split, 2 cas. Answers the failed swaps (cas) or 0.
(:: addThread (-> Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (addThread cell n mode)
  (let (
    (mut i 0)
    (mut failed 0)
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (if (== mode 0)
            (__atomic_add cell 1)
            (if (== mode 1)
              (__atomic_store cell (+ (__atomic_load cell) 1))
              (let ((mut old (__atomic_load cell)))
                (while (!= (__atomic_cas cell old (+ old 1)) old)
                  {
                    (set failed (+ failed 1))
                    (set old (__atomic_load cell))
                  }))))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      failed
    }))

(:: runAdd (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runAdd mode n)
  (let ((cell (__alloc 8)))
    (parallel p (
      (a (addThread cell n mode))
      (b (addThread cell n mode))
    )
      {
        (let ((lost (- (* 2 n) (__atomic_load cell))))
          (println
            (strConcat
              (fmtInt lost)
              (strConcat
                " "
                (fmtInt
                  (if (== mode 2)
                    (+ a b)
                    (* 2 n)))))))
        0
      })))

; One result line, `<forbidden> <witnessed>`.
(:: report (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (report forbidden witnessed)
  {
    (println (strConcat (fmtInt forbidden) (strConcat " " (fmtInt witnessed))))
    0
  })

; ---- lb ------------------------------------------------------------
; mode 0 sc, 1 plain, 3 reorder. Loads round i's word of `src` into
; res[i], then stores 1 to round i's word of `dst`. `reorder` stores
; first, with the atomics.
(:: lbThread (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (lbThread src dst res ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 0)
            (let ((r (__atomic_load (+ src (* 8 i)))))
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ dst (* 8 i)) 1)
                (__store64 res i r)
              })
            (if (== mode 1)
              (let ((r (__load64 src i)))
                {
                  (__store64 dst i 1)
                  (__store64 res i r)
                })
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ dst (* 8 i)) 1)
                (__store64 res i (__atomic_load (+ src (* 8 i))))
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; Forbidden is both loads answering 1; the witness is the rounds in
; which both answered 0, so both loads ran before either store landed.
(:: runLb (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runLb mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r0 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut both 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (lbThread
          xs
          ys
          r0
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (lbThread
          ys
          xs
          r1
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (let ((s (+ (__load64 r0 i) (__load64 r1 i))))
            (if (== s 2)
              (set weak (+ weak 1))
              (if (== s 0)
                (set both (+ both 1))
                0)))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak both)
    }))

; ---- 2+2w ----------------------------------------------------------
; mode 0 sc, 1 plain, 3 reorder. Stores 1 to round i's word of `first`,
; then 2 to `second`'s. `reorder` stores in the other order, with the
; atomics.
(:: twoThread (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (twoThread first second ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 0)
            {
              (__atomic_store (+ first (* 8 i)) 1)
              (__atomic_store (+ second (* 8 i)) 2)
            }
            (if (== mode 1)
              {
                (__store64 first i 1)
                (__store64 second i 2)
              }
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ second (* 8 i)) 2)
                (__atomic_store (+ first (* 8 i)) 1)
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; T0 stores x 1 then y 2, T1 stores y 1 then x 2. Read after the join,
; forbidden is x 1 with y 1; the witness is x 2 with y 2, the rounds in
; which the two threads' stores interleaved.
(:: runTwo (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runTwo mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut both 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (twoThread
          xs
          ys
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (twoThread
          ys
          xs
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (let (
            (x (__load64 xs i))
            (y (__load64 ys i))
          )
            (if (&& (== x 1) (== y 1))
              (set weak (+ weak 1))
              (if (&& (== x 2) (== y 2))
                (set both (+ both 1))
                0)))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak both)
    }))

; ---- iriw ----------------------------------------------------------
; Arrive at round `round`'s barrier and wait until all `parties` have.
; After 2,048 spins it waits on the word for up to 2 us at a time, so a
; host with fewer cores than parties still makes progress. Much sooner
; loses the rounds' overlap: at 64 spins, `iriw plain` at --opt 0
; stopped showing its outcome on darwin-aarch64, and at 256 an --opt 2
; run took seven to nine times as long.
(:: arriveAll (-> Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (arriveAll ctr round parties)
  (let (
    (mut spins 0)
    (want (* parties (+ round 1)))
  )
    {
      (__atomic_add ctr 1)
      (let ((mut seen (__atomic_load ctr)))
        (while (< seen want)
          {
            (set spins (+ spins 1))
            (if (> spins 2048)
              (sysWaitWordTimeout ctr seen 2000)
              0)
            (set seen (__atomic_load ctr))
          }))
      spins
    }))

; How long `reorder`'s writers pause between a word's two copies.
(:: pauseSpins Int)
(fn (pauseSpins)
  64)

; How many loads `reorder`'s wrc reader spends waiting for the relay.
(:: waitSpins Int)
(fn (waitSpins)
  4096)

; Load `w` until it is non-zero, at most `k` times. Answers the loads
; made.
(:: waitStored (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (waitStored w k)
  (let ((mut j 0))
    {
      (while (&& (< j k) (== (__atomic_load w) 0))
        (set j (+ j 1)))
      j
    }))

; Spin `k` atomic loads of `w`, which the optimiser cannot remove.
(:: pause (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (pause w k)
  (let (
    (mut j 0)
    (mut sum 0)
  )
    {
      (while (< j k)
        {
          (set sum (+ sum (__atomic_load w)))
          (set j (+ j 1))
        })
      sum
    }))

; mode 0 sc, 1 plain, 3 reorder. Stores 1 to round i's word of `near`.
; `reorder` then pauses and stores 1 to `far`'s too: one write reaching
; the two readers' copies at different times.
(:: iriwWriter (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (iriwWriter near far ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arriveAll ctr i 4)
          (if (== mode 1)
            (__store64 near i 1)
            (if (== mode 0)
              (__atomic_store (+ near (* 8 i)) 1)
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ near (* 8 i)) 1)
                (pause ctr pauseSpins)
                (__atomic_store (+ far (* 8 i)) 1)
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; mode 1 plain; every other mode with the atomic loads. Loads round i's
; word of `first`, then of `second`, and writes 2 * first + second to
; res[i]: 2 means this reader saw `first`'s write and not `second`'s.
(:: iriwReader (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (iriwReader first second res ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arriveAll ctr i 4)
          (if (== mode 1)
            (let ((f (__load64 first i)))
              (__store64 res i (+ (* 2 f) (__load64 second i))))
            (let ((f (__atomic_load (+ first (* 8 i)))))
              (__store64 res i (+ (* 2 f) (__atomic_load (+ second (* 8 i)))))))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

(:: count2 (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (count2 res n)
  (let (
    (mut i 0)
    (mut c 0)
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (if (== (__load64 res i) 2)
            (set c (+ c 1))
            0)
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      c
    }))

; Four bindings: W0 stores x, W1 stores y, R2 loads x then y, R3 loads
; y then x. Forbidden is R2 seeing x without y while R3 sees y without
; x: the readers disagree on the order of the writes. The witness is
; the rounds showing the rarer half of that, R2's or R3's, so both
; orders are seen, if never in the same round. `reorder` gives each
; reader its own copy of the other writer's word, written after a
; pause, so W0 reaches R2 first and W1 reaches R3 first.
(:: runIriw (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runIriw mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (xFar (if (== mode 3)
      (__alloc (* 8 n))
      xs))
    (yFar (if (== mode 3)
      (__alloc (* 8 n))
      ys))
    (ra (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (rb (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (iriwWriter
          xs
          xFar
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (iriwWriter
          ys
          yFar
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (c (iriwReader
          xs
          yFar
          ra
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (d (iriwReader
          ys
          xFar
          rb
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a (+ b (+ c d))))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (if (&& (== (__load64 ra i) 2) (== (__load64 rb i) 2))
            (set weak (+ weak 1))
            0)
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (let (
        (ha (count2 ra n))
        (hb (count2 rb n))
      )
        (report
          weak
          (if (< ha hb)
            ha
            hb)))
    }))

; ---- wrc and isa2 ----------------------------------------------------
; mode 1 plain, 0 sc, 3 reorder. Stores 1 to round i's word of `first`,
; then of `second`; `reorder` stores `second` first, pauses, then stores
; `first` (isa2's writer; wrc's writes one word and passes 0 as `second`).
(:: chainWriter (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (chainWriter first second ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arriveAll ctr i 3)
          (if (== mode 1)
            {
              (__store64 first i 1)
              (if (== second 0)
                0
                (__store64 second i 1))
            }
            (if (|| (== mode 0) (== second 0))
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ first (* 8 i)) 1)
                (if (== second 0)
                  0
                  (__atomic_store (+ second (* 8 i)) 1))
              }
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ second (* 8 i)) 1)
                (pause ctr pauseSpins)
                (__atomic_store (+ first (* 8 i)) 1)
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; Loads round i's word of `src` into res[i], then stores 1 to `dst`'s.
(:: chainRelay (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (chainRelay src dst res ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arriveAll ctr i 3)
          (if (== mode 1)
            (let ((v (__load64 src i)))
              {
                (__store64 dst i 1)
                (__store64 res i v)
              })
            (let ((v (__atomic_load (+ src (* 8 i)))))
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ dst (* 8 i)) 1)
                (__store64 res i v)
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; Loads round i's word of `first` into rf[i], then `second`'s into
; rs[i]. `reorder` loads `second` first, then waits for `first` to be
; stored, for at most `waitSpins` loads, and loads it. Waiting for the
; store rather than pausing a fixed time keeps the control's outcome
; visible on a host whose relay is slower than a fixed pause: with a
; 64-load pause, linux-aarch64 at -O2 showed wrc's in none of 5 runs.
(:: chainReader (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (chainReader first second rf rs ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arriveAll ctr i 3)
          (if (== mode 1)
            (let ((a (__load64 first i)))
              {
                (__store64 rs i (__load64 second i))
                (__store64 rf i a)
              })
            (if (== mode 3)
              (let ((b (__atomic_load (+ second (* 8 i)))))
                {
                  (waitStored (+ first (* 8 i)) waitSpins)
                  (__store64 rf i (__atomic_load (+ first (* 8 i))))
                  (__store64 rs i b)
                })
              (let ((a (__atomic_load (+ first (* 8 i)))))
                {
                  (__store64 rs i (__atomic_load (+ second (* 8 i))))
                  (__store64 rf i a)
                })))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; Counts the rounds in which r1 and r2 both answered 1 (the chain), and
; among them the rounds in which r3 answered 0 (forbidden).
(:: chainTally (-> Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (chainTally r1 r2 r3 n)
  (let (
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut chain 0)
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (if (&& (== (__load64 r1 i) 1) (== (__load64 r2 i) 1))
            {
              (set chain (+ chain 1))
              (if (== (__load64 r3 i) 0)
                (set weak (+ weak 1))
                0)
            }
            0)
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak chain)
    }))

; W stores x; R1 loads x, stores y; R2 loads y, then x. `reorder` is
; R2's: it loads x first.
(:: runWrc (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runWrc mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r2 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r3 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (chainWriter
          xs
          0
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (chainRelay
          xs
          ys
          r1
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (c (chainReader
          ys
          xs
          r2
          r3
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a (+ b c)))
      (chainTally r1 r2 r3 n)
    }))

; W stores x, then y; R1 loads y, stores z; R2 loads z, then x.
; `reorder` is W's and R2's: W stores y first and x after a pause, and
; R2 loads x first and z once R1 has stored it. W's alone raced R1's
; relay against the pause, and on linux-aarch64, where the relay was
; slower, the control showed nothing at -O1 and -O2 in 5 runs (CI runs
; 36570497827 and 36577299489). Either reordering alone lets
; sequential consistency give the outcome; the control only shows the
; harness can see it.
(:: runIsa2 (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runIsa2 mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (zs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r2 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r3 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (chainWriter
          xs
          ys
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (chainRelay
          ys
          zs
          r1
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (c (chainReader
          zs
          xs
          r2
          r3
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a (+ b c)))
      (chainTally r1 r2 r3 n)
    }))

; ---- coherence --------------------------------------------------------
; Round i's word of x: a plain load under mode 1, otherwise an atomic one.
(:: loadAt (-> Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (loadAt x i mode)
  (if (== mode 1)
    (__load64 x i)
    (__atomic_load (+ x (* 8 i)))))

; Round i's word of x set to v: plainly under mode 1, otherwise atomically.
(:: storeAt (-> Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (storeAt x i v mode)
  {
    (if (== mode 1)
      (__store64 x i v)
      (__atomic_store (+ x (* 8 i)) v))
    0
  })

; The storing side: round i's word of x gets `v`, then, a pause later,
; `w`. `reorder` stores `w` first and `v` second. A `w` of 0 means one
; store. mode 1 plain, 0 sc, 3 reorder.
(:: cohWriter (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
(fn (cohWriter x v w ctr n mode)
  (let (
    (mut i 0)
    (first (if (&& (== mode 3) (!= w 0))
      w
      v))
    (second (if (&& (== mode 3) (!= w 0))
      v
      w))
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (storeAt x i first mode)
          (if (== second 0)
            0
            {
              (pause ctr pauseSpins)
              (storeAt x i second mode)
            })
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; Two loads of round i's word of x, a pause apart, into r1[i] then
; r2[i]; `swap` 1 reports the later load as r1, corr's reordering.
(:: cohReader (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (cohReader x r1 r2 swap ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (let ((a (loadAt x i mode)))
            {
              (pause ctr pauseSpins)
              (let ((b (loadAt x i mode)))
                (if (== swap 1)
                  {
                    (__store64 r1 i b)
                    (__store64 r2 i a)
                  }
                  {
                    (__store64 r1 i a)
                    (__store64 r2 i b)
                  }))
            })
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; One store of 1 and one load of round i's word of x, a pause apart,
; the load's answer into r1[i]. `own` 1 stores then loads (cowr), 0
; loads then stores (corw); `reorder` swaps the two.
(:: cohSelf (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (cohSelf x r1 own ctr n mode)
  (let (
    (mut i 0)
    (storeFirst (if (== own 1)
      (if (== mode 3)
        0
        1)
      (if (== mode 3)
        1
        0)))
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== storeFirst 1)
            {
              (storeAt x i 1 mode)
              (pause ctr pauseSpins)
              (__store64 r1 i (loadAt x i mode))
            }
            (let ((a (loadAt x i mode)))
              {
                (pause ctr pauseSpins)
                (storeAt x i 1 mode)
                (__store64 r1 i a)
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; corr: W stores 1; R loads twice. Forbidden 1 then 0; witness 0 then 1.
(:: runCorr (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runCorr mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r2 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut both 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (cohWriter
          xs
          1
          0
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (cohReader
          xs
          r1
          r2
          (if (== mode 3)
            1
            0)
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (let (
            (a (__load64 r1 i))
            (b (__load64 r2 i))
          )
            (if (&& (== a 1) (== b 0))
              (set weak (+ weak 1))
              (if (&& (== a 0) (== b 1))
                (set both (+ both 1))
                0)))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak both)
    }))

; coww: W stores 1 then 2; R loads twice. Forbidden R seeing 2 then 1,
; or x not ending with W's last store; witness R seeing x change.
(:: runCoww (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runCoww mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r2 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (last (if (== mode 3)
      1
      2))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut moved 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (cohWriter
          xs
          1
          2
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (cohReader
          xs
          r1
          r2
          0
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (let (
            (a (__load64 r1 i))
            (b (__load64 r2 i))
          )
            {
              (if (|| (&& (== a 2) (== b 1)) (!= (__load64 xs i) last))
                (set weak (+ weak 1))
                0)
              (if (!= a b)
                (set moved (+ moved 1))
                0)
            })
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak moved)
    }))

; cowr (own 1) and corw (own 0): W stores 1 and loads, in the order
; `own` says; O stores 2. Forbidden: W's load answering what coherence
; excludes for its own store (0 for cowr, 1 for corw, counted except
; under `reorder`), or 2 while x ends as it cannot (1 for cowr, 2 for
; corw). The witness is the rounds in which W read O's 2.
(:: runCoSelf (-> Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runCoSelf own mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (ownBad (if (== own 1)
      0
      1))
    (endBad (if (== own 1)
      1
      2))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut saw 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (cohSelf
          xs
          r1
          own
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (cohWriter
          xs
          2
          0
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (let ((r (__load64 r1 i)))
            {
              (if (|| (&& (== r 2) (== (__load64 xs i) endBad)) (&& (!= mode 3) (== r ownBad)))
                (set weak (+ weak 1))
                0)
              (if (== r 2)
                (set saw (+ saw 1))
                0)
            })
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak saw)
    }))

; ---- r and s -----------------------------------------------------------
; T0 of both: stores `v` to round i's word of `first`, then `w` to
; `second`'s. mode 1 plain, 2 fence (plain, with `__fence` between),
; otherwise the atomics.
(:: pairWriter (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (pairWriter first v second w ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 1)
            {
              (__store64 first i v)
              (__store64 second i w)
            }
            (if (== mode 2)
              {
                (__store64 first i v)
                __fence
                (__store64 second i w)
              }
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ first (* 8 i)) v)
                (__atomic_store (+ second (* 8 i)) w)
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; r's T1: stores 2 to round i's word of y, then loads x's into res[i].
; `reorder` loads x first, then stores 2 once T0's store to y is
; visible, waiting for at most `waitSpins` loads.
(:: rThread (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (rThread xs ys res ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 1)
            {
              (__store64 ys i 2)
              (__store64 res i (__load64 xs i))
            }
            (if (== mode 2)
              {
                (__store64 ys i 2)
                __fence
                (__store64 res i (__load64 xs i))
              }
              (if (== mode 3)
                (let ((r (__atomic_load (+ xs (* 8 i)))))
                  {
                    (waitStored (+ ys (* 8 i)) waitSpins)
                    (__atomic_store (+ ys (* 8 i)) 2)
                    (__store64 res i r)
                  })
                {
                  (__atomic_store (+ ys (* 8 i)) 2)
                  (__store64 res i (__atomic_load (+ xs (* 8 i))))
                })))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; s's T1: loads round i's word of y into res[i], then stores 1 to x's.
; `reorder` stores x first, then loads y once T0's store to it is
; visible, waiting for at most `waitSpins` loads.
(:: sThread (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (sThread xs ys res ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arrive ctr i)
          (if (== mode 1)
            (let ((r (__load64 ys i)))
              {
                (__store64 xs i 1)
                (__store64 res i r)
              })
            (if (== mode 2)
              (let ((r (__load64 ys i)))
                {
                  __fence
                  (__store64 xs i 1)
                  (__store64 res i r)
                })
              (if (== mode 3)
                {
                  (__atomic_store (+ xs (* 8 i)) 1)
                  (waitStored (+ ys (* 8 i)) waitSpins)
                  (__store64 res i (__atomic_load (+ ys (* 8 i))))
                }
                (let ((r (__atomic_load (+ ys (* 8 i)))))
                  {
                    (__atomic_store (+ xs (* 8 i)) 1)
                    (__store64 res i r)
                  }))))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; Counts the rounds in which `fin`'s word ended `fv` and res[i] answered
; `rv` (forbidden), and those in which they ended `wf` and `wr`
; (witnessed), and reports both.
(:: pairTally (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (pairTally fin res fv rv wf wr n)
  (let (
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut both 0)
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (let (
            (f (__load64 fin i))
            (r (__load64 res i))
          )
            (if (&& (== f fv) (== r rv))
              (set weak (+ weak 1))
              (if (&& (== f wf) (== r wr))
                (set both (+ both 1))
                0)))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak both)
    }))

; r: T0 stores x then y; T1 stores 2 to y, then loads x. Forbidden is y
; ending 2 with T1's load answering 0; the witness is y ending 1 with
; the load answering 1, the rounds whose accesses interleaved.
(:: runR (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runR mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (res (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (pairWriter
          xs
          1
          ys
          1
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (rThread
          xs
          ys
          res
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (pairTally
        ys
        res
        2
        0
        1
        1
        n)
    }))

; s: T0 stores 2 to x, then 1 to y; T1 loads y, then stores 1 to x.
; Forbidden is x ending 2 with T1's load answering 1; the witness is x
; ending 1 with the load answering 0, the rounds whose accesses
; interleaved.
(:: runS (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runS mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (res (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (pairWriter
          xs
          2
          ys
          1
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (sThread
          xs
          ys
          res
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a b))
      (pairTally
        xs
        res
        2
        1
        1
        0
        n)
    }))

; ---- 3.sb --------------------------------------------------------------
; Load `w` until it reaches `want`, at most `k` times. Answers the loads
; made.
(:: waitCount (-> Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (waitCount w want k)
  (let ((mut j 0))
    {
      (while (&& (< j k) (< (__atomic_load w) want))
        (set j (+ j 1)))
      j
    }))

; mode 0 sc, 1 plain, 3 reorder. Stores 1 to round i's word of `mine`,
; then loads `next`'s into res[i]. `reorder` loads first, adds 1 to
; round i's word of `gate`, waits for all three bindings to have, for at
; most `waitSpins` loads, then stores.
(:: sb3Thread (-> Int Int Int Int Int Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (sb3Thread mine next res gate ctr n mode)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (arriveAll ctr i 3)
          (if (== mode 1)
            {
              (__store64 mine i 1)
              (__store64 res i (__load64 next i))
            }
            (if (== mode 3)
              (let ((r (__atomic_load (+ next (* 8 i)))))
                {
                  (__atomic_add (+ gate (* 8 i)) 1)
                  (waitCount (+ gate (* 8 i)) 3 waitSpins)
                  (__atomic_store (+ mine (* 8 i)) 1)
                  (__store64 res i r)
                })
              {
                (__atomic_store (+ mine (* 8 i)) 1)
                (__store64 res i (__atomic_load (+ next (* 8 i))))
              }))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      0
    }))

; T0 stores x, loads y; T1 stores y, loads z; T2 stores z, loads x.
; Forbidden is all three loads answering 0; the witness is all three
; answering 1, the rounds in which every store preceded every load.
(:: runSb3 (-> Int Int Int))
;@axiom:effect(io)
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(fn (runSb3 mode n)
  (let (
    (xs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (ys (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (zs (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r0 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r1 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (r2 (__alloc (* 8 n)))
    (gate (if (== mode 3)
      (__alloc (* 8 n))
      0))
    (ctr (__alloc 8))
    (mut i 0)
    (mut weak 0)
    (mut full 0)
  )
    {
      (parallel p (
        (a (sb3Thread
          xs
          ys
          r0
          gate
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (b (sb3Thread
          ys
          zs
          r1
          gate
          ctr
          n
          mode))
        (c (sb3Thread
          zs
          xs
          r2
          gate
          ctr
          n
          mode))
      )
        (+ a (+ b c)))
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (let ((s (+ (__load64 r0 i) (+ (__load64 r1 i) (__load64 r2 i)))))
            (if (== s 0)
              (set weak (+ weak 1))
              (if (== s 3)
                (set full (+ full 1))
                0)))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      (report weak full)
    }))

(:: modeOf (-> String Int))
(fn (modeOf s)
  (if (strEq s "sc")
    0
    (if (|| (strEq s "plain") (strEq s "split"))
      1
      (if (|| (strEq s "fence") (strEq s "cas"))
        2
        (if (strEq s "reorder")
          3
          (- 0 1))))))

(:: usage Int)
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (usage)
  {
    (println "usage: atomics (sb sc|plain|fence) | (add sc|split|cas) | (mp|r|s sc|plain|fence|reorder) | (3.sb|lb|2+2w|iriw|wrc|isa2|corr|coww|cowr|corw sc|plain|reorder)")
    2
  })

(:: main Int)
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let (
    (family (sysArg 1))
    (mode (modeOf (sysArg 2)))
    (n (if (|| (strEq family "iriw") (|| (strEq family "wrc") (|| (strEq family "isa2") (strEq family "3.sb"))))
      200000
      500000))
  )
    (if (< mode 0)
      (usage)
      (if (&& (strEq family "sb") (< mode 3))
        (runSb mode n)
        (if (strEq family "mp")
          (runMp mode n)
          (if (&& (strEq family "add") (< mode 3))
            (runAdd mode n)
            (if (strEq family "r")
              (runR mode n)
              (if (strEq family "s")
                (runS mode n)
                (if (&& (strEq family "3.sb") (!= mode 2))
                  (runSb3 mode n)
                  (if (&& (strEq family "lb") (!= mode 2))
                    (runLb mode n)
                    (if (&& (strEq family "2+2w") (!= mode 2))
                      (runTwo mode n)
                      (if (&& (strEq family "iriw") (!= mode 2))
                        (runIriw mode n)
                        (if (== mode 2)
                          (usage)
                          (if (strEq family "wrc")
                            (runWrc mode n)
                            (if (strEq family "isa2")
                              (runIsa2 mode n)
                              (if (strEq family "corr")
                                (runCorr mode n)
                                (if (strEq family "coww")
                                  (runCoww mode n)
                                  (if (strEq family "cowr")
                                    (runCoSelf 1 mode n)
                                    (if (strEq family "corw")
                                      (runCoSelf 0 mode n)
                                      (usage))))))))))))))))))))
